  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35733932",
      "title": "Data Fetching with a loader()",
      "sourceHash": "54639a855b067d293ec251aa19c5b645b81918599464bf4bb60cdca062d14a9f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 5.55,
          "en": "We are now ready to dive deeper into Routing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.55,
          "end": 9.81,
          "en": "and explore more advanced features of React router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.81,
          "end": 14.22,
          "en": "And one of the most important feature sets offered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 14.22,
          "end": 18.3,
          "en": "by React router is related to data fetching and submission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 18.3,
          "end": 20.823,
          "en": "and that's there for what we'll explore next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 21.87,
          "end": 25.68,
          "en": "For that attached, you find a new file Events.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 25.68,
          "end": 29.43,
          "en": "which you should use to replace your Events.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 29.43,
          "end": 31.47,
          "en": "in the pages folder with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 31.47,
          "end": 35.46,
          "en": "And once you replaced your Events.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 35.46,
          "end": 36.96,
          "en": "with the provided one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.96,
          "end": 41.07,
          "en": "and you then explore this Eventsjs file, you will see that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.07,
          "end": 46.02,
          "en": "in that file there is some code that sends an http request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.02,
          "end": 50.76,
          "en": "to that dummy backend api, which I'm providing to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 50.76,
          "end": 54.42,
          "en": "And you should make sure that that backend API server is up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 54.42,
          "end": 56.91,
          "en": "and running in a separate terminal window",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 56.91,
          "end": 59.193,
          "en": "as shown a couple of lectures ago.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 60.39,
          "end": 63.54,
          "en": "And then that response is evaluated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 63.54,
          "end": 65.52,
          "en": "An error is stored with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.52,
          "end": 69.39,
          "en": "of state if it's a invalid response, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 69.39,
          "end": 73.28999999999999,
          "en": "because we got an error back from the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 73.28999999999999,
          "end": 76.74,
          "en": "If we don't have an error, we instead extract the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 76.74,
          "end": 80.73,
          "en": "from the response and store that with help of state as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 80.73,
          "end": 82.89,
          "en": "And we're all managing the loading state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.89,
          "end": 85.59,
          "en": "And then all these states are used down here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.59,
          "end": 88.62,
          "en": "to either show a loading text, an error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 88.62,
          "end": 91.11,
          "en": "or to render the fetched events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.11,
          "end": 93.87,
          "en": "which are now fetched from the dummy backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.87,
          "end": 97.22999999999999,
          "en": "some dummy event data from the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.22999999999999,
          "end": 99.47999999999999,
          "en": "Those events are rendered here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.47999999999999,
          "end": 102,
          "en": "with help of that events list component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102,
          "end": 104.4,
          "en": "which exists to this components folder already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.4,
          "end": 105.36,
          "en": "So, which was part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.36,
          "end": 107.97999999999999,
          "en": "of that starting project I provided earlier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.17,
          "end": 112.08,
          "en": "and this code should look familiar to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.08,
          "end": 113.25,
          "en": "Fraud discourse,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.25,
          "end": 117,
          "en": "you already learned how you can send http requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117,
          "end": 120.21,
          "en": "to a backend and how you can leverage useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.21,
          "end": 122.22,
          "en": "to fetch data from a backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.22,
          "end": 124.563,
          "en": "So this should be familiar code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.52,
          "end": 128.22,
          "en": "Now, there is nothing wrong with debt code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.22,
          "end": 132.45,
          "en": "but of course it is worth noting that it's quite some",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.45,
          "end": 135.84,
          "en": "boiler plate code, which you have to repeat every time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.84,
          "end": 138.69,
          "en": "you are sending a request to a backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.69,
          "end": 140.94,
          "en": "Though you could kind of mitigate that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.94,
          "end": 144.3,
          "en": "by creating a custom hook and you could outsource that logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.3,
          "end": 145.74,
          "en": "into a custom hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.74,
          "end": 148.89,
          "en": "But nonetheless, it's quite some code that must be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.89,
          "end": 153.09,
          "en": "written to handle these different http request states",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.09,
          "end": 155.52,
          "en": "and to fetch that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.52,
          "end": 158.46,
          "en": "And in addition, what's all the worth noting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 158.46,
          "end": 161.56,
          "en": "is that of course this request will only be sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 161.56,
          "end": 164.16,
          "en": "once we reached this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 164.16,
          "end": 167.19,
          "en": "So once we navigate it to this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 167.19,
          "end": 168.99,
          "en": "this is by the way how it looks like,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 168.99,
          "end": 171.69299999999998,
          "en": "this is the data fetched from this dummy backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 172.56,
          "end": 174.57,
          "en": "So we only start sending that request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 174.57,
          "end": 176.76,
          "en": "as soon as we reach the events page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.76,
          "end": 179.64,
          "en": "We don't start sending the request any earlier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.64,
          "end": 181.83,
          "en": "instead only once we reach this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 181.83,
          "end": 182.88,
          "en": "And that of course means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 182.88,
          "end": 185.497,
          "en": "that this entire events page component must be rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 185.497,
          "end": 188.193,
          "en": "before this request is sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.6,
          "end": 191.76,
          "en": "That's not necessarily a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 191.76,
          "end": 195.33,
          "en": "And here it is a pretty straightforward, simple component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 195.33,
          "end": 197.576,
          "en": "But of course, in more complex applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 197.576,
          "end": 200.91,
          "en": "this component could be rather complex",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 200.91,
          "end": 204.39,
          "en": "and it could also have a bunch of nested child components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 204.39,
          "end": 208.675,
          "en": "and having to render and evaluate all these components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 208.675,
          "end": 213.03,
          "en": "before we actually start sending that request for that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 213.03,
          "end": 217.38,
          "en": "which we absolutely need, is suboptimal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.38,
          "end": 220.32,
          "en": "You could argue that it would be much nicer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 220.32,
          "end": 224.57999999999998,
          "en": "if React router would initiate the data fetching as soon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 224.57999999999998,
          "end": 227.1,
          "en": "as we start navigating to this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 227.1,
          "end": 230.88,
          "en": "So as soon as we start rendering this component, so to say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 230.88,
          "end": 233.778,
          "en": "or even before we render the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 233.778,
          "end": 235.74,
          "en": "and we then render the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 235.74,
          "end": 237.475,
          "en": "with the fetched data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 237.475,
          "end": 240.27,
          "en": "instead of first rendering the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 240.27,
          "end": 241.83,
          "en": "without the fetched data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 241.83,
          "end": 244.26,
          "en": "with the loading state fallback instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 244.26,
          "end": 245.31,
          "en": "and then fetching data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 245.31,
          "end": 248.58,
          "en": "after it has been rendered as it's currently happening.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 248.58,
          "end": 251.25,
          "en": "It could be preferable to do it the other way around",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 251.25,
          "end": 255.66,
          "en": "and first fetched the data and then render this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 255.66,
          "end": 259.05,
          "en": "And that's exactly what React router allows us to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 259.05,
          "end": 262.05,
          "en": "And where React router helps us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 262.05,
          "end": 265.44,
          "en": "With React router at least if you're using version six",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 265.44,
          "end": 268.8,
          "en": "or higher you don't have to write all that code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 268.8,
          "end": 271.89,
          "en": "for fetching data and for handling these different states.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 271.89,
          "end": 275.355,
          "en": "Instead, React router helps you with all of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 275.355,
          "end": 276.96,
          "en": "And it helps you with all of that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 276.96,
          "end": 279.48,
          "en": "by giving you an extra property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 279.48,
          "end": 282.243,
          "en": "which you can add to your route definitions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 283.14,
          "end": 285.84000000000003,
          "en": "Now we're currently talking about this events page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 285.84000000000003,
          "end": 288.51,
          "en": "That's this page where we're fetching data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 288.51,
          "end": 292.77,
          "en": "and in our route definitions we can add an extra property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 292.77,
          "end": 295.74,
          "en": "to that route definition of that page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 295.74,
          "end": 298.773,
          "en": "We can add the extra loader property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 299.79,
          "end": 304.79,
          "en": "Now, loader is a property that wants a function as a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 304.83,
          "end": 306.09,
          "en": "a regular function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 306.09,
          "end": 309.243,
          "en": "or an error function that does not matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 310.08,
          "end": 312.27,
          "en": "And this function will be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 312.27,
          "end": 315.12,
          "en": "by a React router whenever you are about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 315.12,
          "end": 317.49,
          "en": "to visit this route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 317.49,
          "end": 320.01,
          "en": "So just before this route gets rendered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 320.01,
          "end": 322.41,
          "en": "just before this JSX code gets rendered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 322.41,
          "end": 324.81,
          "en": "this loader function will be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 324.81,
          "end": 327.84,
          "en": "and executed by a React router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 327.84,
          "end": 331.41,
          "en": "And it's in this loader function where you can therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 331.41,
          "end": 334.02,
          "en": "load and fetch your data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 334.02,
          "end": 335.90999999999997,
          "en": "So we can go back to events JS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 335.90999999999997,
          "end": 339.36,
          "en": "and grab this code where we fetch the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 339.36,
          "end": 342.27,
          "en": "and where we evaluate the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 342.27,
          "end": 347.073,
          "en": "and cut that and instead move it into this loader function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 347.97,
          "end": 350.13,
          "en": "Now, we will need to tweak this a little bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 350.13,
          "end": 352.35,
          "en": "to make the code work though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 352.35,
          "end": 354.99,
          "en": "For example, we should add the async keyword here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 354.99,
          "end": 357.6,
          "en": "so that we can use the await keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 357.6,
          "end": 360.45,
          "en": "Alternatively, we could of course add the then method here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 360.45,
          "end": 362.1,
          "en": "since Thatcher returns a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 362.1,
          "end": 365.16,
          "en": "but async a weight is a bit easier to read.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 365.16,
          "end": 368.43,
          "en": "We also don't need to set any state values here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 368.43,
          "end": 369.993,
          "en": "so we get rid of all of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 371.28,
          "end": 373.47,
          "en": "Instead here, we'll deal with that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 373.47,
          "end": 376.5,
          "en": "incorrect response case later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 376.5,
          "end": 378.06,
          "en": "and we'll focus on the scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 378.06,
          "end": 380.343,
          "en": "that we do have a valid response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 381.27,
          "end": 383.46,
          "en": "In that case, we got the response data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 383.46,
          "end": 384.93,
          "en": "in this loader function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 384.93,
          "end": 387.36,
          "en": "And of course, we wanna get that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 387.36,
          "end": 389.31,
          "en": "to that events page component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 389.31,
          "end": 391.443,
          "en": "because that's where we need the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 392.46,
          "end": 393.78,
          "en": "Well, the great thing is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 393.78,
          "end": 396.54,
          "en": "that when you define such a loader function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 396.54,
          "end": 399.99,
          "en": "React router will automatically take any value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
